# Test fixture, not a build input.
#
# A handful of suites under tests/ parse SHAs out of a pins file to assert
# their own parsing logic, to name the commit their C++-as-text assertions
# are about (they read src/mod_overseer.cpp via the mod-overseer/ submodule
# below), and to check a vendored patch header still quotes a currently
# pinned upstream SHA. This is a vendored SNAPSHOT of
# quadseven/infra's production/docker/azerothcore-playerbots/UPSTREAM-PINS.env
# for that purpose only - it does not drive any build here, and nothing here
# reads AC_CORE_REPO/AC_CLIENT_DATA_VERSION/etc. for a build the way infra
# does.
#
# THE AUTHORITATIVE FILE is infra's copy. Keep AC_OVERSEER_SHA here equal to
# this repo's own mod-overseer/ submodule pin (see .gitmodules / `git -C
# mod-overseer rev-parse HEAD`) - a mismatch between the two is exactly the
# drift infra#3093 was written to catch, just relocated: there it was
# pin-vs-gitlink-vs-checkout inside one repo, here it is this repo's
# submodule vs whatever infra separately pins. Nothing currently automates
# keeping the REST of this file in sync with infra's copy; it is refreshed
# by hand when a test that reads it needs a real value.
#
# Below this line: infra's UPSTREAM-PINS.env, copied verbatim as of
# 2026-09-18 (the day of this repo's extraction), with AC_OVERSEER_SHA
# refreshed to 2026-09-20's value when infra#4224's promotion was carried
# across (it is the one line here a test depends on being current).

# Upstream pins for the AzerothCore + mod-playerbots images.
#
# WHY TWO REPOS: mod-playerbots does NOT build against upstream AzerothCore.
# It requires the module authors' own core fork, on the `Playerbot` branch,
# which carries the AI hooks the module binds to. Upstream AzerothCore will
# not compile with it. (Stated by mod-playerbots' own README; verified
# 2026-08-20.)
#
# WHY SHAs AND NOT BRANCH NAMES: `Playerbot` and `master` are moving targets.
# A branch-tracking build makes the image non-reproducible and turns an
# upstream regression into a mystery rebuild failure. Bump these deliberately.

AC_CORE_REPO=https://github.com/mod-playerbots/azerothcore-wotlk.git
AC_CORE_SHA=47960183bb03b83e8943eb2f0f39c16df9710c9d

AC_MODULE_REPO=https://github.com/quadseven/mod-playerbots.git
AC_MODULE_SHA=60e6555e4e4b552ee4c6551b466aff648916f38b

# --- Additional modules, compiled into the same worldserver ---------------
AC_OLLAMA_CHAT_REPO=https://github.com/DustinHendrickson/mod-ollama-chat.git
AC_OLLAMA_CHAT_SHA=8ba5e791f0a84ee04636f0b19b62d3c4aff3dce1

AC_DUNGEON_CLEAR_REPO=https://github.com/quadseven/mod-dungeon-clear.git
AC_DUNGEON_CLEAR_SHA=b9bdae002a2bb2fbfc464075819c85a2a793e426

AC_JUNK_TO_GOLD_REPO=https://github.com/noisiver/mod-junk-to-gold.git
AC_JUNK_TO_GOLD_SHA=2134690bb03899e5c9e44d0682e8e6abf0bbbaf2

# mod-overseer's own pin. Keep equal to this repo's mod-overseer/ submodule.
AC_OVERSEER_REPO=https://github.com/quadseven/mod-overseer.git
AC_OVERSEER_SHA=a41766ea4883c55787f0f3f6b7f0337cca39ea4f

AC_AH_BOT_REPO=https://github.com/NathanHandley/mod-ah-bot-plus.git
AC_AH_BOT_SHA=f685832994c825f90aa5a3dc0e1620aa568e875b

AC_CLIENT_DATA_VERSION=v20.0
